==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|ML.|-}} {{m|la|registrārius}}, from {{m|la|registrum||register}} + {{m|la|-ārius||agent}}. See more at {{m|en|register}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛd͡ʒ.ɪsˌtɹɑɹ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-registrar.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[official]] [[keeper]] or [[recorder]] of [[record]]s.
## An [[officer]] in a [[university]] who keeps [[enrollment]] and [[academic]] [[achievement]] records.
## {{lb|en|museums}} The person responsible for record-keeping related to a museum's or archive's collection.
## {{lb|en|law}} The [[chief executive officer]] of a judicial forum, in charge of the entire registry of the department.
# A [[doctor]] receiving [[advanced]] [[specialist]] [[training]] in some [[countries]] in order to become a [[consultant]].
# {{lb|en|Internet}} A [[service]] that [[manage]]s the [[reservation]] of [[domain name]]s.

